  takeaways: ['Drive-reduction: restore homeostasis. Arousal theory: Yerkes-Dodson optimal arousal. Incentive: external pull.', 'Maslow: physiological → safety → belonging → esteem → self-actualization.', 'Ghrelin increases hunger; leptin reduces appetite; the hypothalamus regulates eating.', 'James-Lange: arousal then emotion; Cannon-Bard: simultaneous; Schachter-Singer: arousal + label; Lazarus: appraisal first.', 'The amygdala drives fear; the prefrontal cortex regulates emotion.'],
